        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "On the pilot, the LLM agrees with a human coder on the relevance of 97 percent of the articles, the same rate as between two human coders.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The numbers match Tables 3 and 4 (33 of 34 in both). Section 4 states that with only 34 articles, of which 3 were coded relevant by the pilot coder, the sample is too small to test whether the agreement rates differ and that results are indicative only. Table 4 shows 30 of the 33 agreements are on not-relevant articles, and the LLM flagged 4 articles as relevant against the pilot coder's 3. The abstract and the introduction restate the parity without this qualification.",
